{
  "title": "Distal Radial Ulnar Joint (DRUJ) Injuries",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/trauma/1028/distal-radial-ulnar-joint-druj-injuries",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Feb 15 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Introduction",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Frequently occur with distal radius fractures but must be considered independently",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "common cause of **pain and limited ROM** after distal radius fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "often underappreciated and ignored",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**ulnar styloid and distal ulna fractures**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**TFCC tears**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**ulnar impaction syndrome**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Essex-Lopresti injuries**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Galeazzi fractures**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "DRUJ",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "arthrology",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "articulation occurs between the ulnar head and sigmoid notch (a shallow concavity found along ulnar border of distal radius)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "most stable in **supination**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "primary stabilizers",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**volar and dorsal radioulnar ligaments**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1028/images/druj_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "distal oblique bundle of the interosseous membrane may serve as a primary stabilizer to the DRUJ in cases of injury of these structures",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**TFCC**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1028/images/tfcc.jpg",
                      "caption": "Shows the anatomy of the TFCC"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "TFCC attaches to the fovea at the base of the ulnar styloid",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "components include",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "central articular disc",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "meniscal homologue",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "volar and dorsal radioulnar ligaments",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "ulnolunate and ulnotriquetral ligament origins",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "floor of the ECU tendon sheath",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "biomechanics",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "joint motion includes both rotation and translation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**pain and instability** with acute DRUJ dislocation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "associated with open distal radius fractures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "dorsal wrist pain and **limited pronosupination** with post-traumatic arthritis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "post-traumatic arthritis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "snapping and crepitus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "proximal rotation of the forearm with compression of the ulna against the radius elicits pain",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "decreased grip strength",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1028/images/druj%20instability.jpg",
              "caption": "Show the radiographic features of DRUJ instability"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "AP shows **widening of the DRUJ**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "lateral shows **dorsal displacement**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "instability of the DRUJ is present when the ulnar head is subluxed from the sigmoid notch by its full width with the arm in neutral rotation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Dynamic CT",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "useful in the diagnosis of subtle chronic DRUJ instability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "sequential CT scans are performed with the forearm in neutral and full supination and pronation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": ">50% translation compared to the contralateral side is abnormal",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "useful in the identification of TFCC injuries",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1028/images/tfcc%20mri.jpg",
                  "caption": "Shows a vertical tear of the volar radioulnar ligament component of the TFCC."
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "closed reduction, immobilization",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "DRUJ instability resulting from purely ligamentous injury",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "techniques",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "closed reduction and immobilization in a position of stability for 4 weeks",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "dorsal instability is stable with the forearm in supination",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "volar instability is stable in pronation",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "interposition of ECU may impede closed reduction",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "DRUJ pinning, radioulnar ligament repair",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "highly unstable DRUJ",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "techniques",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "pinning across joint with 0.062-inch K-wires",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ulnar Styloid Fractures",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Reflects **high degree of initial fracture displacement**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Fractures through base often associated with TFCC rupture and instability",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "In the absence of instability, ulnar styloid nonunions are not associated with worse outcomes",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "nonoperative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "cast immobilization",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "nondisplaced fractures proximal to the ulnar styloid",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "operative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "ORIF, symptomatic fragment excision",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**displaced fractures through the base** with associated instability",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "sigmoid notch fractures",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "Galeazzi fracture patterns",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "TFCC avulsions in the face of an unstable DRUJ",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "techniques",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "preserve ulnar attachments of TFCC with fragment excision",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "TFCC Tears",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Etiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Mechanism of injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "wrist extension, forearm pronation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "in pronation, volar ligaments prevent dorsal subluxation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "in supination, dorsal ligaments prevent volar subluxation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Classification",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "type I - traumatic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "type II - degenerative (ulnocarpal impaction)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "IIA - TFCC thinning",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "IIB - IIA + lunate and/or ulnar chondromalacia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "IIC - IIB + TFCC perforation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "IID - IIC + LT ligament disruption",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "IIE - IID + ulnocarpal and DRUJ arthritis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "nonoperative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "immobilization, NSAIDS",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "all acute traumatic TFCC tears",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "operative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "arthroscopic vs. open debridement and/or repair",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "failure of nonoperative management",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "persistent symptoms",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "techniques",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "type I injuries",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "arthroscopic vs. open debridement and/or repair",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "type II injuries",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "TFCC pathology treated with arthroscopic or open debridement",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "ulnocarpal impaction treated with ulnar shortening osteotomy (in the absence of DRUJ arthrosis) or wafer resection of the ulnar head",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ulnar Impaction Syndrome",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radial shortening leads to **positive ulnar variance** and altered mechanics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Sequelae includes",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**lunate chondromalacia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**degenerative TFCC tears**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative treatment",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "TFCC debridement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "radial osteotomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "ulnar shortening",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "distal ulnar resection (Wafer procedure)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "preserve ulnar attachment of TFCC",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Essex-Lopresti Injuries",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radial head fracture with an **interosseous membrane injury extending to DRUJ**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1028/images/essex-lopresti%20injury.jpg",
              "caption": "Shows an Essex-Lopresti injury"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "unstable relationship between ulna and radius",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "leads to **proximal migration of the radius**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "results in **secondary DRUJ pathology** and ulnocarpal abutment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "treat bony pathology (radial head or shaft)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**pin DRUJ for 6 weeks** in neutral to facilitate ligamentous healing",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "if pinning fails (or the initial injury is missed) radial head replacement may be required",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Galeazzi Fractures",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Distal one-third fracture of the radius and a DRUJ injury",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "ECU entrapment may cause DRUJ to be irreducible",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "nonoperative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "splint in supination",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "rarely indicated for stable injuries",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "operative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "radial ORIF and DRUJ pinning",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "often required to achieve a stable reduction",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**DRUJ arthrosis**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "treatment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "resection arthroplasty (resect distal ulna)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "matched resection vs. Darrach",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "Darrach procedure",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [
                            {
                              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1028/images/darrach%20procedure.jpg",
                              "caption": "Shows a Darrach procedure"
                            }
                          ],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "reserved for low-demand, elderly patients",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "1",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "an unstable, painful proximal ulna stump may result",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "1",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "hemiresection or interposition arthroplasty",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "ulnar insertion of TFCC is preserved",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "radioulnar impingement is prevented by soft tissue interposition",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "Sauve-Kapandji procedure",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1028/images/sauve-kapandji%20pa%20and%20lateral.jpg",
                      "caption": "Shows a Sauve-Kapandji procedure"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "DRUJ fusion with creation of a proximal ulnar neck pseudoarthrosis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "ulnar head prosthetic replacement",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "creation of a one-bone forearm",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "ultimate salvage procedure that eliminates forearm rotation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Primary method to prevent disability related to DRUJ injuries is **anatomic reduction of the distal radius** which often results in an anatomically-reduced DRUJ",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
